message: "If you use FlowMLLab, please cite the archived v1.0.0 software release and the associated SoftwareX article."
title: "FlowMLLab: An Open-Source Framework for Reproducible CFD-to-Scientific-Machine-Learning Experiments"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roohi
    given-names: Ehsan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5739-3210"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ehsan-Roohi/FlowMLLab"
url: "https://github.com/Ehsan-Roohi/FlowMLLab/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22073935"
    description: "Archived FlowMLLab v1.0.0 software release"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  FlowMLLab integrates transparent continuum and particle solvers, case-wise
  data partitions, non-neural baselines, coordinate networks, POD-DeepONet
  models, physical diagnostics, machine-readable validation evidence, and
  release-quality assurance for reproducible scientific machine learning in
  fluid mechanics.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - scientific machine learning
  - neural operators
  - direct simulation Monte Carlo
  - reproducibility
